# =============================================================================
# LearnCraft .dockerignore  (AUTHORITATIVE)
# =============================================================================
# Both supported build commands use the REPOSITORY ROOT as the build context
# (`docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` / compose `context: ..`), and Docker
# always reads `<context>/.dockerignore`. This file is therefore the one that
# actually applies; docker/.dockerignore only documents the same intent.
#
# What must never reach an image:
#   - backend/.secret_key  (session signing key generated by run_server.*)
#   - any .env             (LEARNCRAFT_SECRET_KEY, mail/AI credentials)
#   - *.db / *.sqlite3     (local SQLite with real accounts + logs)
#
# PATTERN RULE: Docker matches with Go filepath.Match, where `*` does NOT cross
# a `/`. Every rule that must apply at ANY depth therefore uses a `**/` prefix
# (e.g. `**/*.db` or `backend/data/*.db` would both work; plain `*.db` only
# matches a file at the context root and silently let the real database into
# the image before this was fixed).
# =============================================================================

# Python bytecode / packaging (any depth)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info/
*.egg

# Virtual environments (repo root venv/ and backend/.venv/)
**/.venv/
**/venv/
backend/.venv/

# Secrets and local configuration (any depth)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.docker.example
**/.secret_key
backend/.secret_key

# SQLite databases and sidecars (mounted at runtime instead).
# NOTE: do NOT exclude `backend/data/` as a directory — it is source code
# (data/seed/*.py + curriculum JSON that app.main imports at boot). Exclude
# only the database files themselves, at any depth.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# IDE / editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.code-workspace

# Logs and temp files (any depth)
**/*.log
server.err.log
server.log
server_err.log
server_out.log
tmp/
temp/

# Testing / coverage caches
**/.pytest_cache/
**/ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Build artifacts / archives
*.zip
*.tar.gz
dist/
build/

# Documentation (operators read it from the repo, not from the image)
docs/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
